course: dictionary
lesson: 12077
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word show you which meaning the writer wants. «Mia held her clipboard and wrote down each bird she saw.» Mia is writing while she walks, so the clipboard must be the flat board with a clip that holds paper.
explain: «Sam clicked copy, then clicked paste.» There is no paper here. Copy and paste are computer actions, so the clipboard is the hidden place in the computer that holds what was copied. Always ask: what do the other words tell me?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If the sentence still makes sense and fits the clues, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A clipboard is a flat board with a metal clip at the top that holds sheets of paper.
fact: You can write on paper held by a clipboard while you stand or walk, which makes it useful outside.
fact: On a computer or phone, the clipboard is a hidden place that stores what you have copied or cut.
fact: Copied text or pictures stay on the clipboard until you paste them somewhere else.
fact: On field trips, nature walks and surveys, clipboards are often used to make tally charts.
exercise: «Mia held her clipboard and wrote down each bird she saw.» In this sentence, what is a clipboard? | A box for keeping pencils | A kind of bird | A hidden place in a computer that stores copied text | *A flat board with a metal clip that holds paper
exercise: «Sam clicked copy, then clicked paste.» Where is the copied text kept until it is pasted? | On the desk | In the printer tray | In the bin | *In the clipboard
exercise: Ms Lee says, «Take your clipboard and count the cars that pass the school gate.» What does clipboard mean here? | A board game with counters | *A flat board with a metal clip for holding paper | A large blackboard at the front of the class | A computer's hidden storage place
test: Mark writes tally marks on his clipboard as he walks around the park. Why does he use a clipboard? | *To hold paper so he can write while walking | To measure how long the park is | A place to store copied text | To keep his lunch warm
test: «Press Ctrl+C to copy, then Ctrl+V to paste from the clipboard.» What does the clipboard do in this sentence? | It holds sheets of paper with a metal clip | *It stores the copied text until you paste it | It plays music | It shows the time on the screen
exam: «The clipboard was empty, so nothing could be pasted.» What does clipboard mean here? | A flat board with a clip for paper | A tray for lunch | *A hidden place in a computer that stores copied items | A map of the school
